{"step_index":260,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T21:10:50Z","content":"Quick math using NexLev data:\n\n**Known facts:**\n- Total lifetime views: **3,238,849**\n- This month's views: **2,227,269**\n- Channel RPM: **\\$6.07**\n- Channel age: **~8.5 months**\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 1: Remove THIS month's views\n\n| | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Views before this month | 3,238,849 − 2,227,269 = **1,011,580** |\n| Earnings before this month | 1,011,580 × \\$6.07 ÷ 1000 = **\\$6,140** |\n| Months before this one | ~7.5 months |\n| **Avg monthly earning (before spike)** | **\\$819/month** |\n\n### Scenario 2: Remove LAST 2 months' views\n\n| | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Views from first 6.5 months | 1,011,580 views (over 7.5 months), minus ~1 more month ≈ **~876,703** *(estimated)* |\n| Earnings from first 6.5 months | 876,703 × \\$6.07 ÷ 1000 ≈ **\\$5,322** |\n| **Avg monthly earning (first 6.5 months)** | **~\\$819/month** |\n\n---\n\n### The Real Story:\n\n| Period | Monthly Views | Monthly Earnings |\n|--------|-------------|-----------------|\n| **First 7.5 months** (before spike) | ~135K/month | **~\\$819/month** |\n| **This month** (the spike) | 2,227,269 | **\\$13,118** |\n\n> **68.8% of ALL lifetime views came in just THIS month.** Before the current spike, Just Explained was earning ~\\$819/month — decent but not huge. The algorithm picked it up recently and views went from ~135K/month → 2.2M/month (**16x jump**).\n\nThat's the real picture — without this month's spike, it was a **\\$800/month channel**, not a \\$13K channel.","thinking":"The user wants to know for Just Explained:\n1. Lifetime income MINUS this month's views (i.e., what did he earn before this month's spike)\n2. Lifetime income MINUS last 2 months' views\n\nLet me calculate:\n\nTotal views: 3,238,849\nChannel RPM: $6.07\nMonthly views (current): 2,227,269\n\n**Scenario 1: Remove 1 month's views**\n- Remaining views: 3,238,849 - 2,227,269 = 1,011,580\n- Earnings from remaining: 1,011,580 × $6.07 / 1000 = $6,140.29\n- That's spread over roughly 7.5 months, averaging about $818.71/month.\n\nFor the second scenario, I don't have exact views for the month before last, so I'm trying subtracting twice the current month's views from the total, but that overshoots since 2×2,227,269 exceeds the total — meaning the channel likely didn't have two months at this current view level.\n\nSo realistically the current month accounts for over two-thirds of all-time views, and without a second month's actual data, I can only reliably calculate the \"remove 1 month\" scenario: subtracting current month views from total leaves 1,011,580 views across the remaining months, yielding roughly $6,140 in earnings.\n\nFor removing two months, I don't have last month's data isolated, so I'll go with the straightforward one-month removal calculation ($6,140 in earnings, 7.5 months, ~$819/month average) as the clearest answer, since estimating a two-month split would require assumptions not supported by the data."}
